Encephalitis Lethargica Due to
Epstein–Barr Virus Infection
There is circumstantial evidence to suggest that sporadic
encephalitis lethargica (EL) might be a postinfectious immu-
nological disorder affecting gray matter, and in some instan-
ces it may follow a streptococcal infection.
1 MRI in patients
with EL has shown lesions in bilateral substantia nigra com-
patible with the clinical ﬁndings.
1,2 We describe a 20-year-
old woman who was 20 weeks’ pregnant who 1 week after
an upper respiratory tract infection developed parkinsonism,
